WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.173 --> 00:00:02.906
- So, here's the thing,
now, I'm a hustler, okay?

00:00:02.906 --> 00:00:06.960
So I went to New York, no
money. I had one friend there.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.722
I was sleeping on her
couch, and I would take jobs

00:00:09.722 --> 00:00:12.542
at temp agencies to
sort of make ends meet,

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.247
to feed myself, right?

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.407
So, literally, on the corner
of 125th Street and Broadway,

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:18.474
there was a phone booth.

00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:19.792
This is how long ago that was,

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:20.625
you know.
- Yep, phone booth.

00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:22.019
- Phone booth.
- It wasn't a cell phone.

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:23.334
Okay, it was a phone booth.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:26.363
And I would call into the temp
agency every single morning.

00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:27.987
I would start calling them at 7:30,

00:00:27.987 --> 00:00:30.461
call 'em every 15 minutes
until I got a job.

00:00:30.461 --> 00:00:33.778
And like, it took like
six weeks (chuckles)

00:00:33.778 --> 00:00:36.746
for me every single day
calling and then getting a job.

00:00:36.746 --> 00:00:38.146
Finally, it was like the golden day

00:00:38.146 --> 00:00:40.471
when I got a job to be the receptionist

00:00:40.471 --> 00:00:42.303
at Spike's advertising agency.

00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:43.925
- Oh, wow!
- And so I get there,

00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:46.642
and I'm only supposed
to answer the phones.

00:00:46.642 --> 00:00:49.596
Now, I see he's carrying
around something under his arm,

00:00:49.596 --> 00:00:51.600
coming back and forth in the office.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.301
It happened to be the
script for "Bamboozled,"

00:00:54.301 --> 00:00:56.373
and I asked him if I could read it,

00:00:56.373 --> 00:00:58.485
being an African-American studies,

00:00:58.485 --> 00:00:59.842
you know, literature person.

00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:00.675
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:00.675 --> 00:01:01.961
I thought I could perhaps
give him some tips.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.009
(woman laughing)
- You know what I mean?

00:01:03.009 --> 00:01:03.878
- I love it!

00:01:03.878 --> 00:01:04.711
Bold, though.

00:01:04.711 --> 00:01:06.312
- Yeah, and naive. (chuckles)

00:01:06.312 --> 00:01:07.320
- No!

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.213
- But was perfect.

00:01:08.213 --> 00:01:09.066
Because it's like,

00:01:09.066 --> 00:01:11.537
I think today I probably
would've hesitated, right?

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:12.683
I would've been like, "Oh, Spike,

00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:15.157
like how can you even give
him any kind of tips at all?"

00:01:15.157 --> 00:01:16.040
But at the time, I was like,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.356
"Oh yes, I'm gonna do him a favor."

00:01:17.356 --> 00:01:18.574
(Kelly claps)
(audience laughs)

00:01:18.574 --> 00:01:19.460
You know what I mean?

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.293
- Totally.

00:01:20.293 --> 00:01:21.187
- I took the script, I marked it up,

00:01:21.187 --> 00:01:22.848
give it back to him.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:24.887
He looked at me like I
had lost my whole mind,

00:01:24.887 --> 00:01:26.674
(all laughing)
and, no,

00:01:26.674 --> 00:01:27.902
but he looked at it and said,

00:01:27.902 --> 00:01:30.210
"Okay, like, actually you
make some good points.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.800
You should stay here for a while.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:32.633
- Oh gosh.
- That's my gosh that I got.

